course: dictionary
lesson: 7605
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word printer is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context, and they leave clues. «Priya in Leicester said the printer broke, and her teacher said "Lovely, email it tonight then" - there was nothing to email.» A printer that breaks and needs an email to be sent is a machine, so here printer means a machine.
explain: «A 3D printer melts plastic string and lays it down layer by thin layer following a computer drawing.» The clues are melts plastic, layer by layer and computer drawing. A 3D printer builds solid objects, not pages, so this meaning is different again.
explain: «Chinese printers often kept using carved woodblocks, because Chinese needs thousands of different characters.» Here printers are the people or companies who make printed work. They chose a way of printing, so they are not machines. The word around it tells you which meaning to pick.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. «The printer broke» works with machine, and «printers kept using carved woodblocks» works with people or companies whose job is printing. If a meaning does not fit, try the next one.
fact: A printer is a machine that prints words and pictures on paper from a computer.
fact: A printer can also be a person or company whose job is printing books, newspapers or posters.
fact: A 3D printer builds solid objects layer by layer.
fact: Phrases like «printer ink» and «paper jam» are about the machine, so look for them as clues.
fact: In history, the printing press made books cheap, so more people could read them.
exercise: «Priya in Leicester said the printer broke.» What does printer mean here? | A person whose job is printing posters | A bird that sings | *A machine that prints on paper | A kind of paper
exercise: «A 3D printer melts plastic string and lays it down layer by thin layer.» What does a 3D printer do? | Prints words on paper only | Melts ice on a path | Sorts letters in a post office | *Builds solid objects layer by layer
exercise: «Chinese printers often kept using carved woodblocks.» What does printers mean here? | Teachers | *People or companies whose job is printing | Pieces of paper | Computers
test:
Ella says a printer is always a machine. Is she right? | Yes, a printer is always a machine | *No, a printer can also be a person or company whose job is printing | Yes, but only a 3D printer | No, a printer is a kind of food
«Printers use cyan, magenta and yellow instead, which mix cleaner colours.» What do these printers do? | Sing songs | Melt plastic string | *Mix and print colours | Carry letters to houses
exam: Ben reads «Chinese printers often kept using carved woodblocks.» Which meaning fits best? | A paper jam | A machine that sings | *People or companies whose job is printing | A bird
